2186115162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050876 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115163 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050876 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050876 #edb/ref 1031 "Angles and Sides in Right Triangles" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050876 #edb/ref 1033 1597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050876 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "6dc02150-1f8b-5b70-8bbf-3ac48efdef79" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050941 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050941 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050941 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050941 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049959 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050941 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186208740 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050941 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186208741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050941 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186208742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050941 #edb/ref 1031 "Trigonometric Ratios in Right Triangles" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050941 #edb/ref 1033 5981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050941 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "73b63cf5-ad13-5f77-835c-cd4d3e9b30f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078249 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3240" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078249 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $\\sin{\\theta}$, $\\cos{\\theta}$, and $\\tan{\\theta}$ for the triangle below.\n\n![](images/ed/ed11931671711d754241c84981e7cebf12f04bdae56a1c8b26a194a6bf44b7ca.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078249 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "65c52289-9781-5418-b8c6-fb7693aad674" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078249 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember the acronym \"SOH-CAH-TOA.\"\n\n- The sine of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the hypotenuse (S-O-H). Relative to the angle $\\theta$, the opposite side is $\\overline{AC}$, and the hypotenuse is $\\overline{BC}$. Therefore,\n$\\sin{\\theta} = \\dfrac{AC}{BC} = \\dfrac{3}{5}$.\n- The cosine of an angle is equal to the adjacent divided by the hypotenuse (C-A-H). Relative to the angle $\\theta$, the adjacent side is $\\overline{AB}$, and the hypotenuse is $\\overline{BC}$. Therefore,\n$\\cos{\\theta} = \\dfrac{AB}{BC} = \\dfrac{4}{5}$.\n- The tangent of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the adjacent (T-O-A). Relative to the angle $\\theta$, the opposite side is $\\overline{AC}$, and the adjacent side is $\\overline{AB}$. Therefore,\n$\\tan{\\theta} = \\dfrac{AC}{AB} = \\dfrac{3}{4}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078251 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3243" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078251 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{1}{4}$, find the value of $x$.\n\n![](images/f8/f8affbac78c75000d7bbbc8c15508252f7bea0270fdf6cc9c5e5244eb89b505d.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078251 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e012dbd0-341b-5f01-a670-539c472471bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078251 #edb/ref 1074 "The tangent of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the adjacent (T-O-A).\n\nRelative to the angle $\\theta$, the length of the opposite side is $x-1$, and the length of the adjacent side is $2x$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\tan θ &= \\frac{opposite}{adjacent} \\\\\n\\frac{1}{4} &= \\frac{x - 1}{2x} \\\\\n2x &= 4(x - 1) \\\\\n2x &= 4x - 4 \\\\\n2x &= 4 \\\\\nx &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078253 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3245" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078253 #edb/ref 1071 "In the right triangle $\\triangle ABC$, the angle $\\angle A$ is a right angle, and the side lengths are $AB=2$, $AC=\\sqrt{5}$, and $BC=3$. Find $\\tan B$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078253 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c9ac49b1-04df-5cf0-bd38-3bc5b044b612" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078253 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's illustrate the given triangle.\n\n![](images/4e/4e4e2005e31716a09953aed9054cc5796ee915d41d5a9020042984b348e3b743.png)\n\nThe tangent of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the adjacent (T-O-A). Relative to $\\angle B$, the opposite side is $\\overline{AC}$, and the adjacent side is $\\overline{AB}$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\tan{B} &= \\dfrac{AC}{AB} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}. \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078255 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3247" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078255 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\cos\\left(50^\\circ\\right)$. Round the answer to two decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078255 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "81f7e0c1-99bf-5feb-9db2-745595a8b613" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078255 #edb/ref 1074 "Using a calculator, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos (50^{∘}) &= 0.64278... \\approx 0.64\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078537 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078537 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078537 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078537 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186079106 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078537 #edb/ref 1039 "Evaluating Trigonometric Ratios Given a Triangle with Integer Side Lengths" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078537 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186078249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078537 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "eaac3fe1-285b-57ba-956b-66eaf51ded7e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078538 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048702 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078538 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078813 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078538 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078814 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078538 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186079109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078538 #edb/ref 1039 "Evaluating a Trigonometric Ratio Given a Triangle with Non-Integer Side Lengths" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078538 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186078253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078538 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "50c8132c-18c7-5250-a68e-68500bdb926e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078539 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078539 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078539 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078539 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving for a Variable Given a Trigonometric Ratio" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078539 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186078251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078539 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b6359c90-3e3e-54f3-a66b-c8f69058a3a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078540 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078540 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078540 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186079107 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078540 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186079108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078540 #edb/ref 1039 "Evaluating a Trigonometric Function Using a Calculator" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078540 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186078255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078540 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "bcbd6c22-13de-5a61-90b0-38bd478b4f2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078639 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078639 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078639 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078639 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078639 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079475 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078639 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078639 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078639 #edb/ref 1045 "The Trigonometric Ratios" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078639 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186079471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078639 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078639 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "2606d908-5f7c-5e93-840f-c4b49677eeaa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079471 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079471 #edb/ref 1061 454273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079471 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1e8abd38-6d6c-5110-8d68-959bdff3fee0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079471 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186079636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079472 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079472 #edb/ref 1061 454274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079472 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6fdd25c6-2343-577f-a04a-87a707fb66fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079472 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079473 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079473 #edb/ref 1061 454278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079473 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e74f7b83-5514-5f09-862a-b76a91cf0008" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079473 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079474 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079475 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079474 #edb/ref 1061 454282 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079474 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "888c8f74-0025-5309-8287-98284c3460d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079474 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079475 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079475 #edb/ref 1061 454285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079475 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "13831967-c85e-5019-908f-24b534c39b7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079475 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186079638 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079476 #edb/ref 1061 454286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079476 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ce1bf483-f305-5809-bd7a-831475eed974" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079476 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078540 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079636 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's remind ourselves of the names of the sides of a right triangle relative to an angle $\\theta$.\n\n![](images/4c/4cbe48f70bc4bf67600269883c1260cec2181cf01b50a9675c3177b72d7f954b.png)\n\nThe three fundamental trigonometric ratios, **sine**, **cosine**, and **tangent**, represent the ratios of the sides of a right triangle. The ratios are often shortened to $\\sin$, $\\cos$, and $\\tan$, and they are defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\sin(\\theta) &= \\dfrac {\\text{opposite}} {\\text{hypotenuse}}, \\\\[5pt] \\cos(\\theta) &= \\dfrac {\\text{adjacent}} {\\text{hypotenuse}}, \\\\[5pt] \\tan(\\theta) &= \\dfrac {\\text{opposite}} {\\text{adjacent}}. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor a given angle $\\theta$, these ratios remain the same no matter what the size of the triangle is. For example, if we were to double the length of each side of a given triangle, the values of these ratios would remain unchanged.\n\nAn easy way of remembering how to compute the different trigonometric ratios is by using the three-syllable acronym **SOH-CAH-TOA**. It stands for:\n\n- SOH $\\rightarrow$ **S**ine = **O**pposite / **H**ypotenuse,\n- CAH $\\rightarrow$ **C**osine = **A**djacent / **H**ypotenuse,\n- TOA $\\rightarrow$ **T**angent = **O**pposite / **A**djacent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079636 #edb/ref 1065 2445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079636 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7210f33b-b202-57e9-a4c7-8eb1859c0b97" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079636 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079638 #edb/ref 1064 "Calculators usually have a special key that allows us to compute $\\sin\\theta$, $\\cos\\theta$, and $\\tan\\theta$ for some specific value of $\\theta$.\n\nFor example, using a calculator, we can compute the trigonometric ratios for\n\n$$\n\\theta = 30^\\circ\n$$\n\nand get the following results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (30^{∘}) &= 0.5 \\\\\n\\cos (30^{∘}) &= 0.866... \\\\\n\\tan (30^{∘}) &= 0.577..\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** Make sure that the calculator is in degrees mode (instead of radians mode) before you start the computation." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079638 #edb/ref 1065 2448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079638 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a39bc506-d331-5cab-8f8a-576b9841dc2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079638 #edb/ref 1067 "Calculating Sine, Cosine, and Tangent Using a Calculator" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
